<BaseLayout title='About | damienrobson'>
  <h1>A bit about me</h1>
  <p>Hi, I'm Damien, but you can call me Damo.</p>

  <p>
    I'm an accessibility specialist, helping teams build software and websites
    that work seamlessly for everyone - regardless of ability, device, or
    context. Every now and again, I write about what I learn along the way.
  </p>

  <h2>Why I care about accessibility</h2>

  <p>
    For me, digital accessibility isn't just about guidelines and WCAG criteria
    - it's about empathy and equity. Behind every broken screen reader
    experience or unnavigable form is a real person trying to get something
    done.
  </p>

  <p>
    I believe learning accessibility should feel approachable, not overwhelming.
    You don't need to know every technical spec overnight to start making a
    positive impact.
  </p>

  <h2>Beyond the screen</h2>

  <p>
    Want to chat about accessibility, collaborate, or just say hello? Feel free
    to reach out via <a
      href='https://www.linkedin.com/in/damien-r-4b9b37371/'
      target='_blank'
      rel='noreferrer'>my LinkedIn profile (opens in a new tab)</a
    >!
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
